Generated art for journal/living-language-of-crystal.html drops here as PNG.

GROUND AND TEXTURE ONLY. Nothing in this folder may depict a carving.
The works are real objects that sell once each, so a synthesised picture
of one would be a product photograph of something that does not exist.
Every image of a piece is a photograph of that piece and comes from
pieces-data.js.

Wide plates, 1536x1024:
  hero.png      raw amethyst formation rising out of dark still water
  cave.png      a shaft of light across crystal points inside a cave
  nebula.png    amethyst points rising out of shadow
  craft.png     carving tools and stone dust beside an uncut block

Specimens, 1024x1024 each — raw mineral, uncarved:
  specimen-quartz.png        specimen-amethyst.png    specimen-citrine.png
  specimen-aquamarine.png    specimen-smoky-quartz.png

Every image is masked to a soft edge by the page, so generate on a plain
dark ground and do not compose to a border — the corners are thrown away.
A missing file hides its own element, so the page stays seamless while
this folder is empty.
